{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\n`[verify] plan_review_engine` is a first-class, permanent setting. Both plan-review engines, the 4-pass pipeline and the single read-only agent, stay supported, and this key selects between them (operator decision, 2026-11-12). The setting must be handled like rebar's other settings.\n\nTwo things still mark it as temporary:\n- **How it passes the mechanism ratchet.** 104 other `config_key` and `feature_flag` settings are admitted through entries in `.github/mechanism-baseline.json`, for example `config_key::verify.max_ticket_description_chars`. This key has no baseline entry. It is admitted only by a sunset marker, `src/rebar/_config_sections.py:57` (`# mechanism-ok: config_key verify.plan_review_engine — bossy-impish-hoiho`). By the rules in `src/rebar/_commands/sunset_markers.py`, that marker keeps `bossy-impish-hoiho` from ever closing.\n- **Wording that calls it temporary:**\n  - `src/rebar/_config_sources.py:361`: \"The engine-switch sunset ticket removes the entry.\"\n  - `rebar.toml:34`: \"Sunset with the switch: bossy-impish-hoiho.\"\n  - `docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md:40-41`: the Lifetime bullet.\n  - `docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md:136`: the Consequences bullet.\n\nIts documentation already follows the settings convention: a row in the generated `docs/config-reference.md`, an entry in the `docs/config.md` key inventory, `rebar.toml`, and `docs/plan-review-gate.md`.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. **Admit the key like the other settings.** Add `\"config_key::verify.plan_review_engine\": 1` to `.github/mechanism-baseline.json`, in sorted position among the other `config_key::verify.*` entries. Delete the `# mechanism-ok:` marker at `src/rebar/_config_sections.py:57`.\n\n   **Prerequisite:** AGENTS.md forbids contributors from editing the baseline by hand. This step proceeds only after an explicit operator authorization is recorded as a comment on this ticket. Record that authorization in the commit message body.\n\n   If a test or CI check rejects the baseline growth, stop and report it. Do not work around it or add a marker.\n2. **Reword the `_config_sources.py` comment.** The `_ENV_EXCLUDED_KEYS` entry becomes permanent: the key deliberately takes no environment override, per the ADR 0123 decision of 2026-11-09, which is unchanged.\n3. **Reword the `rebar.toml` comment** and drop its sunset clause.\n4. **Amend ADR 0123:**\n   - Replace the Lifetime bullet with a statement that the key is permanent and both engines are supported.\n   - Reword the Consequences bullet to say both engines are maintained as supported options.\n   - Add a dated 2026-11-12 amendment note recording the change of intent.\n\n   The ADR stays Accepted.\n5. **Check the settings docs** (`docs/config.md`, `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `docs/cli-reference.md`) and remove any sunset or retirement wording. Bring the key's entry in line with how sibling `verify.*` keys are documented there. If `docs/config-reference.md` is affected, regenerate it with `scripts/gen_config_reference.py` rather than editing it by hand.\n\nNo behavior changes: the key, its `pipeline` default, both engines and the environment-variable exclusion all stay as they are.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` contains `config_key::verify.plan_review_engine`, and no `# mechanism-ok:` marker for that key remains in `src`.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] `git grep -n -iE 'bossy-impish-hoiho|sunset' -- src rebar.toml docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md docs/config.md docs/plan-review-gate.md docs/cli-reference.md` prints no line about the engine switch.\n- [ ] ADR 0123 states that the key is permanent and both engines are supported, and carries a dated 2026-11-12 amendment note.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] After the change merges, `bossy-impish-hoiho` is closed with `--class obsolete`, and the command and its output are recorded in a comment on this ticket.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794539899193133882,"uuid":"d27ba2d1-9b85-425d-901d-47d6f54299c9"}